reference[31]: Resolve pending leases after a crash between creating a resource and dibs adopt,"--pending. A resource matches only by evidence recorded before it existed: the","handle pinned with create --name, or the label io.dibs.lease=<id>. Preview by","default. --confirm binds each single unclaimed match. Per lease: bindable, bound,","absent (nothing created; create it now), ambiguous (several matches, never","bound), conflict (match under another lease), unknown (discovery failed).","With <id>: a lease that is no longer pending reports already_done; ambiguous",and conflict exit 3. Unknown exits 1. Age and names never decide a match.,"Examples:","  dibs reconcile","  dibs reconcile <id> --confirm","Output: --axi for agents, --json for scripts (mutually exclusive).","Default: human on terminals; AXI for pipes or DIBS_AXI=1.","Lease commands: --full restores complete AXI records/text; JSON is always complete.","","Contract 1 (reconcile, reclaim, explain, extend, release, and --pending/--key):","exit 0 success with status; 1 operation failed, records retained; 2 usage;","3 refusal, nothing changed, with a stable reason: not_found, wrong_machine,","not_pending, already_leased, key_conflict, handle_exists, handle_mismatch,","resource_absent, resource_unknown, ambiguous, owner_alive, owner_unknown,","expired, owner_dead, job_deadline. Extend success is renewed or reattached.","Exit 1 is only for operation failures. Output carries contract: 1.",See docs/consumer-contract.md.,"","Exit codes: 0 success (including no-ops), 1 operation failed, 2 invalid usage.","dibs job: child's exit code on completion; 124 deadline killed child;",75 (EX_TEMPFAIL) no slot within wait. Dibs's own 1/2 apply only when no child,was started. Signal termination returns 128 + signal number. Helper/wait,failures after start use 125/126 and diagnostics on stderr.,76 is SSH transport/protocol failure with unknown remote result (stderr).,Child exit 255 is preserved and is not confused with SSH failure.
usage: "dibs reconcile [<id>] [--confirm] [--axi | --json]"
